        <body>
            <div xml:id="d387-a2">

                <pb facs="0540" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg438"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign Affairs to Minister
                        Furniss.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-05-20"><hi rendition="#italic">May 20,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 112.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor to inform your
                    excellency that the Haitian Government has decided to put an end to the custom
                    of asylum in legations and consulates established in this country.</p>
                <p>Your legation will kindly take note thereof and issue to your consular agencies
                    precise instructions, that they may strictly comply with that decision.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Louis Borno.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
